    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The Aga Khan University Hospital's Section of Emergency Medicine handles 36,000 patients annually out of which 20 percent are paediatric patients and 15 percent come with cardiac problems. Section of Emergency Medicine provides care to all types of Surgical, Medical, Obstetrical/ Gynecological, Paediatric, Psychiatric and Orthopaedic emergencies. About 60 percent of the totals are medical emergencies, similar to other emergency departments around the world.",
